   "id": "g2-19",
   "name": "Countrysides in Africa: attractive and repulsive aspects"
  }
 ],
 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Attractive aspects (what makes people stay in or move to rural areas):\n• fresh air, quiet and a natural environment;\n• fertile land for farming and cheap or free land;\n• cheap, fresh food;\n• strong family and community ties, traditions and culture;\n• less crime and a lower cost of living.\nRepulsive aspects (what pushes people to leave):\n• few jobs other than farming; low incomes;\n• poor roads, little electricity and pipe-borne water;\n• few secondary schools and hospitals;\n• hard farm work with simple tools, poor harvests and low prices;\n• few leisure activities.\nThe repulsive aspects cause rural exodus (rural–urban migration), mainly of young people. Solutions: build roads, schools, hospitals and electricity in villages; give farmers credit and better tools; create small industries in rural areas.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "x": "a young man leaves his village for Douala"
  },
  "problem": "Give two reasons why {x}.",
  "steps": [
   "In the village there are few jobs besides farming, and incomes are low.",
   "Douala has more jobs, electricity, schools and entertainment."
  ],
  "answer": "Few jobs and services in the village; more chances in the town.",
  "checks": []
 },
